answer 1
error[E0282]: `play` is `@no_alloc`, but `louder` may allocate
  --> no_alloc_through.sisu:20:16
   |
20 |     let loud = louder(samples, 2.0)
   |                ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  = note: `louder` makes a list, at no_alloc_through.sisu:8:12
  = fix: remove `@no_alloc`, so that `play` may allocate

error[E0282]: `play` is `@no_alloc`, but `label` may allocate
  --> no_alloc_through.sisu:22:9
   |
22 |     _ = label(1)
   |         ^^^^^^^^
  = note: `label` builds a `String`, at no_alloc_through.sisu:12:12
  = fix: remove `@no_alloc`, so that `play` may allocate

error[E0282]: `play` is `@no_alloc`, but `tally` may allocate
  --> no_alloc_through.sisu:23:5
   |
23 |     tally(mut seen, 1)
   |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  = note: `tally` grows a list with `push`, at no_alloc_through.sisu:16:5
  = fix: remove `@no_alloc`, so that `play` may allocate

error: Failed
answer 1
error[E0300]: expected `list[int, ref mem.Region]`, found `list[int]`
  --> allocator_mixing.sisu:10:15
   |
10 |     xs.extend(ys)
   |               ^^

error[E0369]: `list[int, ref mem.Region]` and `list[int]` cannot be compared
  --> allocator_mixing.sisu:11:11
   |
11 |     print(xs == ys)
   |           ^^^^^^^^

error[E0351]: `list[int, A]` has no associated function `new`
  --> allocator_mixing.sisu:14:25
   |
14 |     return list[int, A].new()
   |                         ^^^

error: Failed
